I walk over to the bakery.
Fresh rolls and large loaves lie behind the glass.
I wait for my turn.
A baker stands behind the counter.
He looks at me and smiles.
"Hello, what would you like?" he asks.
I point to some dark rolls.
"I would like three rolls, please," I say.
"Yes, of course," says the baker and takes the rolls.
He puts them in a paper bag.
"Anything else?" he asks.
"No thank you, that is all," I answer.
He gives me the bag.
The rolls in the bag are warm.
I look forward to eating them.
